  {
    "id": "2080356308109123753",
    "text": "Hmmm…compression is not about open source per se. Compression is about the limits of knowledge, the use of small parameter proprietary models next to open source large and small parameter models. The idea that humans only have so much knowledge, that the use of that knowledge is limited and often redundant, that these models will become so compressed they will be run on edge compute. It would mean the buildout becomes overbuilt, that AI models are commoditized and customized. It rejects the idea of agent-to agent as of limited practical use and too consumptive of capital and other resources to be anything but carefully executed.",
